\section*{AP \({ }^{\text {® }}\) CALCULUS AB \\ 2008 SCORING GUIDELINES (Form B)}

\section*{Question 4}

The functions \(f\) and \(g\) are given by \(f(x)=\int_{0}^{3 x} \sqrt{4+t^{2}} d t\) and \(g(x)=f(\sin x)\).
\begin{itemize}
\item[(a)] Find \(f^{\prime}(x)\) and \(g^{\prime}(x)\).
\item[(b)] Write an equation for the line tangent to the graph of \(y=g(x)\) at \(x=\pi\).
\item[(c)] Write, but do not evaluate, an integral expression that represents the maximum value of \(g\) on the interval \(0 \leq x \leq \pi\). Justify your answer.
\item[(a)] \(f^{\prime}(x)=3 \sqrt{4+(3 x)^{2}}\)
\[
\begin{aligned}
g^{\prime}(x) & =f^{\prime}(\sin x) \cdot \cos x \\
& =3 \sqrt{4+(3 \sin x)^{2}} \cdot \cos x
\end{aligned}
\]
\item[(b)] \(\quad g(\pi)=0, \quad g^{\prime}(\pi)=-6\)
Tangent line: \(y=-6(x-\pi)\)
\begin{itemize}
\item[] \(4:\left\{\begin{array}{l}2: f^{\prime}(x) \\ 2: g^{\prime}(x)\end{array}\right.\)
\item[] \(2:\left\{\begin{array}{l}1: g(\pi) \text { or } g^{\prime}(\pi) \\ 1: \text { tangent line equation }\end{array}\right.\)
\end{itemize}
\item[3] : \(\left\{\begin{array}{l}1 \text { : sets } g^{\prime}(x)=0 \\ 1 \text { : justifies maximum at } \frac{\pi}{2} \\ 1 \text { : integral expression for } g\left(\frac{\pi}{2}\right)\end{array}\right.\)
\end{itemize}
